      "text": "To solve the inequality \\(\\frac{x^2}{x+1} \\ge \\frac{2}{x-1} + \\frac{5}{4}\\), we first start by combining all terms to one side of the inequality:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2}{x+1} - \\frac{2}{x-1} - \\frac{5}{4} \\ge 0\n\\]\n\nNext, find the least common denominator to combine the fractions. The LCD of \\(x+1\\), \\(x-1\\), and 4 is \\((x+1)(x-1)\\). So, we rewrite the inequality with a common denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2(x-1) - 2(x+1)(x-1) - 5(x+1)(x-1)}{(x+1)(x-1)} \\ge 0\n\\]\n\nSimplify the numerator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2(x-1) - 2(x+1)(x-1) - 5(x+1)(x-1)}{(x+1)(x-1)} = \\frac{x^3 - x^2 - 2(x^2 - 1) - 5(x^2 - 1)}{(x+1)(x-1)}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\frac{x^3 - x^2 - 2x^2 + 2 - 5x^2 + 5}{(x+1)(x-1)}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\frac{x^3 - 8x^2 + 7}{4(x+1)(x-1)}\n\\]\n\nWe can further factor the numerator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^3 - 8x^2 + 7}{4(x+1)(x-1)} = \\frac{(x-1)(x-7)(x+1)}{4(x+1)(x-1)}\n\\]\n\nAssuming \\(x \\neq 1\\), we can cancel the common factors:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(x-7)(x+1)}{4} \\ge 0\n\\]\n\nNow, we analyze the inequality \\(\\frac{(x-7)(x+1)}{4} \\ge 0\\). The critical points where the expression is zero or undefined are \\(x = 7\\) and \\(x = -1\\). These points divide the real number line into three intervals.\n\nTest the sign of the expression in each interval:\n\n1. For \\(x < -1\\), \\((x-7)(x+1)\\) changes sign at points:\n    - \\(x = -6\\), \\((x-7)(x+1) < 0\\), not in the interval.\n    - \\(x = -10\\), \\((x-7)(x+1) > 0\\).\n\n2. For \\(-1 < x < 7\\), \\((x-7)(x+1)\\) changes sign at points:\n    - \\(x = -2\\), \\((x-7)(x+1) > 0\\).\n    - \\(x = 1\\), \\((x-7)(x+1) < 0\\).\n\n3. For \\(x > 7\\), \\((x-7)(x+1)\\) changes sign at points:\n    - \\((x-7)(x+1) > 0\\), \\(x > 7\\).\n\nThus, the inequality \\(\\frac{(x-7)(x+1)}{4} \\ge 0\\) is satisfied when:\n\\[\nx \\le -1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x \\ge 7\n\\]\n\nIncluding the points where the expression is zero:\n\\[\nx = -1, x = 7\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the values of \\(x\\) satisfying the original inequality are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{[-1, \\infty) \\cup (7, \\infty)}\n\\]",
